<https://ontoboard.org/patterns/pmdco-simulation-input-output.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                    dcterms:description "Models information content entities as the input and output of simulation processes. Because BFO roles inhere only in independent continuants, an ICE cannot bear a role directly; the pattern introduces input assignment and output assignment as dependent entities standing for the assignment of an ICE to a process. The example is a division process with numerator and denominator as ICE inputs and a quotient as output."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
                                                                    dcterms:title "Simulation with in- and output"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label moved to skos:prefLabel x2; label added x8; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title \"Simulation with in- and output\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
- header: dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> - https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

